  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="36.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 36.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="36.1" corresp="#wit-h">Gif he ealdermon sy, þolige his scire, buton him se cyning arian wille.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="36.1" corresp="#wit-e">Gif he ealdormon sie, ðolie his scire, buton him kyning arian wille.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="36.1" corresp="#wit-q">Si aldermannus sit, perdat comitatum suum, nisi rex ei parcere uelit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="37.1" corresp="#wit-e">Gif he ealdormon sie, ðolie his scire, buton him kyning arian wille.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e">If he is an <hi rend="italic">ealdorman</hi>, let him forfeit his shire, unless the king is willing to show him mercy.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e">If he is an ealdorman he shall forfeit his shire, unless the king is willing to pardon him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Wenn er Ealdorman ist, verliere er sein Amt, es sei denn, (der) König wolle ihn begnadigen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If he is an ealdorman, let him lose his office, unless (the) king is willing to pardon him.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
